# code.gs contracts

Match the existing `var` / `function` style. Sheet names are exact: `scheme_codes`, `nav_data`.

## Entry points — do not rename
`onOpen` menu **Mutual Fund Matrix**; `showSidebar`; `showDialog` (1250×820); `doGet`; `getFundMatrixData(params)`.

## NAV
`loadNavIndex` reads `nav_data` once per call. `lookupNav` returns the last NAV on or before the date. Do not synthesize NAV and do not cache the sheet in `CacheService`.

## Params
`sipAmount` (1000), `sipDay` (5), `fromDate` (today minus 1 year), `toDate` (today), `saleDate` (today). Dates are `yyyy-MM-dd`.

Custom range: SIP day each month from From through To, redeemed at the To Date NAV. Results: `customRangeXirr`, `sipCorpus`, `netProfit`, `absoluteReturn`, plus `navStart`, `navEnd`, `units`, `investedAmount`. `saleNav` is the Sale Date NAV.

## Tenures (`TENURE_CONFIG`)
Calendar lookbacks from Sale Date. Short: `5D` `15D` `1M` `3M` `6M` `9M` `1Y`. Long: `2Y` `3Y` `5Y` `7Y` `10Y` `12Y`.
`tenureXirr` is annualized. It is `null` when the fund starts after the window, or when the window has no SIP date.
`tenureCagr` is the NAV change over the same window. Under 1Y it is absolute. From 1Y it is annualized. Keep this order identical to the client `TENURES` array.
